# Public documentation (`docs/public`)

## When to update

Update **`docs/public/`** (and `DOCUMENTATION_MANIFEST` in `data/Documentation/documentation-manifest.ts`) when any of these change in a user-visible way:

- Setup flows (tenants, plugins, brands, targets, templates)
- Build phases / steps / gates
- Integrations operators configure or rely on
- Navigation or shell surfaces that change how operators move through the product

## Wording

- **`docs/public/`** — non-developer wording for operators and editors. No stack jargon, no internal file paths as the main instruction.
- **`docs/feature/`** — internal SDLC / engineering plans stay here. Do not move master/sub-plans into `docs/public/`.

## Manifest

Every `docs/public/*.md` file must appear in `DOCUMENTATION_MANIFEST`. Every manifest `file` must exist under `docs/public/`. The Vitest file `manifest.test.ts` enforces both.

## Do not

- Publish engineering-only notes as public guides
- Hardcode long guide copy in React when it belongs in `docs/public/`
- Skip the manifest when adding a new public markdown file
